===========================================scope chain======================================================================================================================
How the Scope Chain Works:
When the JavaScript engine tries to access a variable:
Current Scope First: It starts by searching for the variable in the current (innermost) scope.
Move Up the Chain: If the variable is not found in the current scope, the engine moves up to the immediate outer (parent) scope and continues the search.
Continue to Global Scope: This process continues, traversing the chain of outer scopes, until it reaches the global scope, which is the outermost scope.
ReferenceError: If the variable is not found anywhere in the entire scope chain, a ReferenceError is thrown. 

