Who does tokenization, parsing, AST creation?

👉 V8 itself does it
But not Ignition

Inside V8 there are multiple internal components:
Stage	                V8 Component
Tokenization (Lexing)	V8 Parser
Parsing	                V8 Parser
AST creation	        V8 Parser
Bytecode generation	    V8 (via Ignition pipeline)
Execution	            Ignition (Interpreter)
Optimization	        TurboFan (JIT Compiler)

💡 Ignition does NOT parse
Ignition only executes bytecode

=======================================================================================================================================
The interpreter (Ignition) generates bytecode and starts executing it.
While executing, V8 profiles the code. If some code becomes hot (frequently executed, like loops or repeated function calls), it is sent to the JIT compiler (TurboFan).
TurboFan compiles that bytecode into optimized machine code, which is then executed directly by the CPU, bypassing the interpreter for that part of the code.

